From: usb-proxy appliance <usb-proxy@local>
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: probe the musb gadget controller from board_usb_init

The sunxi musb OTG controller is a UCLASS_USB_GADGET_GENERIC device that nothing
probes on the peripheral path. With !DM_USB_GADGET the sunxi musb gadget has no
DM UDC (usb_add_gadget_udc is #ifndef __UBOOT__), so the DFU/fastboot/UMS flow
reaches it via udc_device_get_by_index(), which in that config just calls
board_usb_init(). sunxi provided none, so the weak no-op ran, the musb glue
never registered its gadget, and dfu/fastboot/ums failed with "Controller
uninitialized" (g_dnl_register -ENXIO). Add a sunxi board_usb_init() that probes
the gadget controller so musb_register() runs and the gadget is available; also
pull in <usb.h> for enum usb_init_type. USB host boot uses the ehci/ohci path
and is unaffected.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
diff --git a/board/sunxi/board.c b/board/sunxi/board.c
index 8c12c8deade..c31b4d11a70 100644
--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #include <init.h>
 #include <log.h>
 #include <mmc.h>
+#include <usb.h>
 #include <axp_pmic.h>
 #include <generic-phy.h>
 #include <phy-sun4i-usb.h>
@@ -678,6 +679,38 @@ int g_dnl_board_usb_cable_connected(void)
 
 	return sun4i_usb_phy_vbus_detect(&phy);
 }
+
+/*
+ * The musb OTG controller is a UCLASS_USB_GADGET_GENERIC device that nothing
+ * probes on the peripheral path: with !DM_USB_GADGET (the sunxi musb gadget has
+ * no DM UDC -- usb_add_gadget_udc is #ifndef __UBOOT__), udc_device_get_by_index()
+ * (drivers/usb/gadget/udc/udc-uclass.c) just calls board_usb_init(). sunxi
+ * provided none, so the weak no-op ran, the musb glue never registered its
+ * gadget, and dfu/fastboot/ums died with "Controller uninitialized"
+ * (g_dnl_register -ENXIO). Probe the controller here so musb_register() runs and
+ * the gadget is available. USB host boot uses the ehci/ohci path, not this.
+ */
+int board_usb_init(int index, enum usb_init_type init)
+{
+	struct udevice *dev;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (init != USB_INIT_DEVICE)
+		return 0;
+
+	ret = uclass_get_device(UCLASS_USB_GADGET_GENERIC, index, &dev);
+	if (ret) {
+		pr_err("%s: cannot find USB gadget controller: %d\n", __func__, ret);
+		return ret;
+	}
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+int board_usb_cleanup(int index, enum usb_init_type init)
+{
+	return 0;
+}
 #endif /* CONFIG_USB_GADGET */
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_SERIAL_TAG
